'''''Gigantochelys''''' ({{lit|giant turtle}}) is an [[extinct]] genus of large [[sea turtle]] in the family [[Dermochelyidae]] known from the [[Late Cretaceous]] ([[Maastrichtian]] age) [[Dakhla Formation]] of Egypt. The genus contains a [[Monotypic taxon|single species]], '''''Gigantochelys aegyptiacus''''', known from bones of the [[pelvis]]. The forelimbs were likely the primary source of propulsion when swimming, but the iliac blade morphology and the robust pubic process of this species indicate that the hindlimbs were likely used more for propulsion than in the [[leatherback sea turtle]], an [[Neontology|extant]] (modern) dermochelyid.<ref name="Gigantochelys" />

